 #define KFX_BITS 5
 inline constexpr int KFX_TAB[2] = { 0x4B465831, KFX_BITS }; // slot 0 magic keeps it out of .bss
+// IGD (Fable/CI spec_igd_1109, b1780 Step 0; 01a1c260 r1452): a plain Issac's gap dash (fight_gap_dash) takes any landing beside a focus
+// he cannot kill. Runtime data flag IGD_TAB[1], read first; 0 = off. Each bit refuses only a dash whose hits don't kill the focus this
+// turn. Bit 1 BAD SPOT: the foes whose one-turn reach covers the landing (the focus, spawn standers and memory <= 3 rounds included) have
+// a summed one-turn burst (two-turn for a foe acting twice before my next turn) >= IGD_RISK % of my eff HP, or of Cassi's when she
+// is visible inside a visible foe's one-turn reach. Bit 4 HURT: my HP < IGD_HP %. (Bit 2 BAG dropped at Step 0: .057/g, no death signal.)
+// Bit 16 (Rule Checker on igd5): the walk-then-dash step at d = dash + 2 (fight_walk_for_dash) is skipped when bits 1/4 would refuse
+// the dash from the step's tile (the landing beside the focus on the step's side), so a refused dash leaves no wasted step into reach.
+// Bit 32 (bit 1b, CI Analyser's exact form; replaces bit 1's test when on): refuse when the burst on my landing leaves me under IGD_RISK %
+// of my eff HP, or the burst of the foes whose one-turn reach covers Cassi's tile, each at its distance to her, leaves her under IGD_RISK %.
+#define IGD_BITS 0
+#define IGD_RISK 40
+#define IGD_HP 60
+inline const volatile int IGD_TAB[4] = { 0x49474431, IGD_BITS, IGD_RISK, IGD_HP }; // slot 0 magic keeps it out of .bss
+#define IGD_ON(b) ((IGD_TAB[1] & (b)) != 0)
